The interesting lines are in dokick.c:

STATIC_OVL void
kickdmg(mon, clumsy)
register struct monst *mon;
register boolean clumsy;
{
...
        int kick_skill = P_NONE;

That line says that the default skill to exercise is none.

        if (dmg > 0) {
                /* convert potential damage to actual damage */
                dmg = rnd(dmg);
                if (martial()) {
                    if (dmg > 1) kick_skill = P_MARTIAL_ARTS;
                    dmg += rn2(ACURR(A_DEX)/2 + 1);
                }

The check for martial arts increases the damage
and also says that a combat skill is involved.

                /* a good kick exercises your dex */
                exercise(A_DEX, TRUE);
        }

But at least kicking is beneficial anyways.  Exercising
dexterity is good until you've max it out and after
that it keeps pushing you back towards max.

        /* may bring up a dialog, so put this after all messages */
        if (kick_skill != P_NONE)       /* exercise proficiency */
            use_skill(kick_skill, 1);

There's the test that registers the skills use if
you're a martial arts users and not otherwise.

So for other character types, only hand-to-hand combat
that uses hands not feet effect the hand-to-hand combat
skill.  Also dexterity is exercised for all character
types.


